From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahnaf Shahriar <ahnaf.shahriar@neuralink.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NRF52840_PPI: Make event-to-task propagation synchronous

The upstream PPI model defers task writes via
ExecuteInNearestSyncedState(), which queues them for the next quantum
boundary sync phase.  This introduces 1-2 quantum delays for what is
a zero-cycle combinational path on real hardware.

For the nRF SoftDevice's radio scheduler, the critical chain is:

  RTC0 COMPARE -> PPI -> TIMER0 Start + RADIO TxEn

With deferred propagation, the CPU can observe stale RADIO/TIMER0
state for up to 2 full quanta after the RTC event fires.  At quantum
sizes > 1us, this causes the SoftDevice to miss its timing windows
and enter error recovery (SVCall loop).

Making the sysbus writes synchronous is safe because PPI callbacks
fire from ClockSource timer handlers at quantum boundaries, which is
the same context used for all peripheral MMIO.  This decouples
correctness from quantum size, matching real hardware behavior.

---
 .../Miscellaneous/NRF52840_PPI.cs             | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Miscellaneous/NRF52840_PPI.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Miscellaneous/NRF52840_PPI.cs
index 0ac366307..ea9e0901a 100644
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Miscellaneous/NRF52840_PPI.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Miscellaneous/NRF52840_PPI.cs
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@ private void EventReceived(int id, uint offset)
             if(taskEndpoint[id] != 0)
             {
                 this.Log(LogLevel.Noisy, "Received an event on channel {0} from 0x{1:X}. Triggering task at 0x{2:X}", id, eventEndpoint[id], taskEndpoint[id]);
-                machine.LocalTimeSource.ExecuteInNearestSyncedState(_ => sysbus.WriteDoubleWord(taskEndpoint[id], 1));
+                sysbus.WriteDoubleWord(taskEndpoint[id], 1);
             }
             else
             {
@@ -263,7 +263,7 @@ private void EventReceived(int id, uint offset)
             if(forkEndpoint[id] != 0)
             {
                 this.Log(LogLevel.Noisy, "Received an event on channel {0} from 0x{1:X}. Triggering fork task at 0x{2:X}", id, eventEndpoint[id], forkEndpoint[id]);
-                machine.LocalTimeSource.ExecuteInNearestSyncedState(_ => sysbus.WriteDoubleWord(forkEndpoint[id], 1));
+                sysbus.WriteDoubleWord(forkEndpoint[id], 1);
             }
         }
 
